description:
Implement a DefaultVerifier struct in pkix-path that dispatches to the available algorithm backends by OID. This is the concrete SignatureVerifier used by pkix-chain-simple and serves as the recommended starting point for users who want RustCrypto defaults.

BLOCKED BY: PKIX-gmv (RSA backend) and PKIX-evy (P-256 backend).

Design:
  pub struct DefaultVerifier; (zero-sized, no state)

  impl SignatureVerifier for DefaultVerifier {
    fn verify_signature(...) -> Result<(), signature::Error> {
      match algorithm.oid {
        OID_SHA256_WITH_RSA => rsa_pkcs1v15_sha256::verify(...),
        OID_ECDSA_SHA256    => ecdsa_p256_sha256::verify(...),
        _                   => Err(signature::Error::new()),  // unsupported algorithm
      }
    }
  }

Feature gating: DefaultVerifier is pub only when at least one backend feature is active. Use #[cfg(any(feature = rsa, feature = p256))] or a derived rustcrypto feature.

This struct is what pkix-chain-simple's internal RustCryptoVerifier should delegate to (eliminating the todo!() in its verify_signature). It can also be exported from pkix-chain for users who want the high-level API with default backends.
